  "narration": [
    {
      "t": 0.6,
      "text": "This repository starts at a vendor drop. Everything that came before it is sitting on another branch with no connection to it."
    },
    {
      "t": 6.5,
      "text": "First, which commit is the one with no parent."
    },
    {
      "t": 15.0,
      "text": "Now git is told to stand a different commit in its place whenever it walks history -- one that does know about the older parent. One command, and the shape of it is on screen."
    },
    {
      "t": 24.0,
      "text": "And the log runs straight back through the old work."
    },
    {
      "t": 32.5,
      "text": "Nothing was rewritten to do it. Ask git to ignore the substitution and the two original commits are exactly as they were, same identities and all. A rebase would not leave you that."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Branches named trunk and upstream with other subjects; the task's branches and commits differ."
